From: H3C HM2004-DU FTTR port
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: airoha: hm2004-du: wire up the FMCS FTTR FPGA

Replace the disabled placeholder fmcs node with the real binding.

The wiring is recovered from the stock device tree (the DTB appended to
mtd2_kernel.bin at file offset 0x21fc), which reads:

    fmcs {
        compatible = "h3c,fmcs";
        spi-controller = <0xb>;
        fpga-spi-int-gpio = <0x17>;
        interrupts = <0x0 0x1a 0x1>;
        fpga-load-rst-gpio      = <0x0>;
        fpga-load-cfg-done-gpio = <0x0>;
        fpga-load-flag-gpio     = <0x0>;
        fpga-load-clk-gpio      = <0x0>;
        fpga-load-do-gpio       = <0x0>;
    };

The five fpga-load-* properties are zero in the shipped DTB and no shipped
module reads them: the loader that actually runs, fpga_load.ko, has no
device-tree code at all and drives hard-coded GPIO block bits.  Those bits map
one-to-one onto GPIO numbers, which is how the configuration port below is
derived.  See docs/REVERSE_ENGINEERING.md sections 1 and 6.

The register transport is deliberately left unbound: the SPI controller that
carries chip select 1 is owned by the SPI-NAND driver in this tree and does not
yet serve generic transfers.  See docs/NEXT_STEPS.md.

---
 target/linux/airoha/dts/an7581-h3c-hm2004-du.dts | 39 lines changed
 1 file changed, 35 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/target/linux/airoha/dts/an7581-h3c-hm2004-du.dts b/target/linux/airoha/dts/an7581-h3c-hm2004-du.dts
--- a/target/linux/airoha/dts/an7581-h3c-hm2004-du.dts
+++ b/target/linux/airoha/dts/an7581-h3c-hm2004-du.dts
@@ -129,10 +129,41 @@
 	 *       status = "okay";
 	 *   };
 	 */
-	fmcs {
-		compatible = "h3c,fmcs";
-		status = "disabled";
-	};
+	fmcs {
+		compatible = "h3c,fmcs";
+
+		/*
+		 * The FPGA interrupt arrives through the pinctrl's GPIO
+		 * interrupt controller, not the GIC directly: the stock node
+		 * names GIC SPI 26, which is exactly the interrupt
+		 * en7581_pinctrl claims for itself in an7581.dtsi.
+		 */
+		interrupt-parent = <&en7581_pinctrl>;
+		interrupts = <23 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+
+		/*
+		 * FPGA configuration port, driven once at probe by the driver's
+		 * bitstream loader.  ACTIVE_HIGH throughout, because the vendor
+		 * shifts raw bit values rather than using inverted logic.
+		 */
+		nconfig-gpios   = <&en7581_pinctrl 5  GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		rst-gpios       = <&en7581_pinctrl 22 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		clk-gpios       = <&en7581_pinctrl 29 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		data-gpios      = <&en7581_pinctrl 30 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		status-gpios    = <&en7581_pinctrl 27 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		conf-done-gpios = <&en7581_pinctrl 28 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+
+		/*
+		 * Runtime register transport.
+		 *
+		 * The FPGA sits on chip select 1 of the SPI controller at
+		 * 0x1fa10000, which this tree hands to the SPI-NAND driver.
+		 * Until that driver serves generic transfers the register path
+		 * cannot bind and only the bitstream load above takes effect.
+		 * See docs/NEXT_STEPS.md.
+		 */
+		status = "okay";
+	};
 };
 
 &en7581_pinctrl {
